From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: restore the ARMv7 assembler and baseline JIT

Upstream deleted the ARMv7 JIT on 2026-08-01. This carries the ARMv7 and
Thumb-2 macro assemblers, registers and disassembler, the 32-bit baseline JIT
(the *32_64.cpp files and the call frame shuffler), and JSValueRegs, so that a
JSValue can live in a register pair. The carried code follows trunk's GC,
profile and register interfaces, has its own signatures for the operations
whose 64-bit form does not fit, profiles arguments the 32-bit way, and does not
lock a profile the JIT writes without the lock.
